From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 19:29:45 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] nfc: st-nci: leave secure element support out when none is
 described

Commit "nfc: st-nci: leave the HCI network alone without a secure
element" returned early from st_nci_discover_se(), but the NCI core still
sends NFCEE_DISCOVER before calling it. Instead, when the device tree
describes neither an eSE nor a UICC, register the NCI device with ops that
have no SE callbacks at all, so power-up touches neither the NFCEEs nor
the HCI network. This replaces the early return.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Derek Ross <derekross@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/nfc/st-nci/core.c | 22 ++++++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 20 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/nfc/st-nci/core.c b/drivers/nfc/st-nci/core.c
index 8c9448db6..ff9fbc408 100644
--- a/drivers/nfc/st-nci/core.c
+++ b/drivers/nfc/st-nci/core.c
@@ -97,6 +97,22 @@ static const struct nci_driver_ops st_nci_prop_ops[] = {
 	},
 };
 
+/*
+ * Without a secure element described there is nothing to discover, and
+ * the HCI network set-up behind SE discovery would clear every pipe in the
+ * controller and replace its session identity, undoing what another host
+ * stack (with its secure element) set up. Leave all of it out.
+ */
+static const struct nci_ops st_nci_ops_no_se = {
+	.init = st_nci_init,
+	.open = st_nci_open,
+	.close = st_nci_close,
+	.send = st_nci_send,
+	.get_rfprotocol = st_nci_get_rfprotocol,
+	.prop_ops = st_nci_prop_ops,
+	.n_prop_ops = ARRAY_SIZE(st_nci_prop_ops),
+};
+
 static const struct nci_ops st_nci_ops = {
 	.init = st_nci_init,
 	.open = st_nci_open,
@@ -135,8 +151,10 @@ int st_nci_probe(struct llt_ndlc *ndlc, int phy_headroom,
 		| NFC_PROTO_NFC_DEP_MASK;
 
 	BUILD_BUG_ON(ARRAY_SIZE(st_nci_prop_ops) > NCI_MAX_PROPRIETARY_CMD);
-	ndlc->ndev = nci_allocate_device(&st_nci_ops, protocols,
-					phy_headroom, phy_tailroom);
+	ndlc->ndev = nci_allocate_device(se_status->is_ese_present ||
+					 se_status->is_uicc_present ?
+					 &st_nci_ops : &st_nci_ops_no_se,
+					 protocols, phy_headroom, phy_tailroom);
 	if (!ndlc->ndev) {
 		pr_err("Cannot allocate nfc ndev\n");
 		return -ENOMEM;
